  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "我不会比你后死吧！”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Surely I will not outlive you, will I!\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "只此寥寥数语。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "There were only these few brief words.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "柏木看了又是怜惜，又是感谢。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "When Kashiwagi read them, he felt both pity and gratitude.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "说道：“呜呼！",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "He said, \"Ah!",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "惟有这‘两烟’一语，是我此生之宝贵遗念。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Only that phrase, 'two wisps of smoke,' is the precious keepsake of this life for me.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "我这一生真虚幻啊！”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "How illusory this life of mine has been!\"",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 7,
      "source_text": "他哭得更加厉害了。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "He wept even more bitterly.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "genji-modern-p03650",
      "unit_index": 8,
      "source_text": "便躺卧在席上写回信，时时搁笔休息，语句断断续续，文字奇奇怪怪，有似鸟的足迹：",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Then he lay on the mat to write his reply, setting down his brush from time to time to rest; the phrases were broken, and the writing was strange, like the tracks of a bird:",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
